When inputs are partitioned by repeated separator rows or columns but demos produce much smaller outputs, dimension ratios help identify possible structure but do not establish the encoding. Keep distinct hypotheses for (a) summarizing interior regions, (b) recording separator/boundary markers at their intersections, and (c) selecting only rows or columns with special markers. For each demo, write down the exact partition counts and map candidate input coordinates or blocks to each output cell, including ordering. Reproduce every output exactly before transferring the map.

After an incorrect compact-output submission, do not merely alter colors or copy another visually salient set of markers. Reopen the task class and output representation, and re-derive dimensions and correspondence from all demos. Repeated, heterogeneous demos may share only an abstract structure; spend another demo only when two explicit mappings predict a materially different discriminating observation.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/USER/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/stage1/H-hermes-luna6-low-ws0/frozen/held-out-2/play/users/u000/system/state/hermes/skills/puzzle-solving/arc-task-delta-inference/references/compact-output-reassessment-after-errors.md"}

{"success": true, "name": "arc-compact-panel-encoding", "file": "references/failed-output-grid-recovery.md", "content": "# Compact-output recovery after rejection

This task demonstrated a costly failure pattern: after a compact panel task's answer was rejected, subsequent answers repeated the same sparse marker interpretation, including duplicate grids, while one attempt accidentally had an invalid row width. Treat each negative result as falsifying the whole candidate rule. Log candidate grids/hypotheses, then derive the compact output dimensions and cell mapping from demos before submitting again. Validate dimensions and row widths separately from the transformation. Do not repeat a candidate or vary only its serialization; a new submission needs a materially different mapping that replays every available demo.
